# Branch preview links

When the user asks for a **preview link** (or "branch build", "try on Pages") for a `cursor/*` branch:

1. **`git fetch origin main`** then **`git rebase origin/main`** on the work branch (resolve conflicts, run targeted tests if needed).
2. **`git push --force-with-lease`** so CI deploys the rebased head.
3. Run **`bash tools/branch-preview-ready.sh`** (or full **`tools/run-harness.sh`**, which includes it) and only share the URL when it passes.
4. Share the preview URL from the script output:
   `https://simmo76.github.io/red-dead-texas-holdem/preview/<branch-with-slashes-as-dashes>/`
   Deploy runs after regression via `deploy-preview.yml` (~2–5 minutes); mention that wait if CI is still running.

Do **not** publish a branch preview link on a `cursor/*` tip that is behind `origin/main` — the UI will look stale (e.g. old HUD stack pill instead of `stack-plaque.png`).